      "sequence_position": 8,
      "problem": "Let $p=⟨3,2,-1⟩$ and $q=⟨6,-1,8⟩.$ Find the vector projection of $q$ onto $p.$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{p}\\,q & =\\frac{p\\cdot q}{p\\cdot p}p \\\\  & =\\frac{{p}_{x}{q}_{x}+{p}_{y}{q}_{y}+{p}_{z}{q}_{z}}{{p}_{x}^{2}+{p}_{y}^{2}+{p}_{z}^{2}}p \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\cdot 6+2\\cdot (-1)+(-1)\\cdot 8}{{3}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}p \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{14}⟨3,2,-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{7}⟨3,2,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{12}{7},\\frac{8}{7},-\\frac{4}{7}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
